{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>They eat.</b> According to the words of the enemies who thought that the burnt offerings are food for the deity, and likewise in plural form according to their words. Therefore it is written: 'I, I am He alone, one, and there is no Elohim with Me.'" "<b>Their wine libations.</b> Like 'and they pour wine' (נסכו יין), and they are two words. Some say: 'the wine of their king' (יין מלכם), like 'the princes of Midian' (נסיכי מדין), for the angel would give the wine of the libation. And the first is closer to me." "<b>And let them rise up.</b> Like 'we have blessed you' (ברכנוכ'), and if you say that it is one word: let them protect you from the troubles coming."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:13.302269351Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}